# What Docker must NOT send when a worker image is built from the repo root.
#
# This is not tidiness. An un-ignored checkout here is about 19 GB, almost all
# of it a Next.js build cache and node_modules that no Python worker imports.
# Docker copies the entire context to the daemon before the first instruction
# runs, so without this file `docker build` appears to hang for many minutes
# and can fill a disk — with no message naming the cause.
#
# Only `workers/county_onramp_worker/Dockerfile` builds from the repo root; the
# other workers build from their own directories and are unaffected.

# Build output and installed dependencies — rebuilt or reinstalled in-image.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.next/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
**/.vercel/
**/.venv/
**/.venv*/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# History and local tooling.
.git/
.github/
.agent-logs/
openplan-worktrees/
.playwright-mcp/

# Secrets never belong in an image layer. The compose file bind-mounts the
# checkout instead, so the worker still reads the real `.env.local` at runtime
# — it is simply never baked in.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Model run outputs and download caches: regenerated on demand, and large.
data/screening-runs/
data/_screening_cache/
workers/aequilibrae_worker/.lodes_cache/
tmp/

# Test and QA scaffolding the workers do not run.
qa-harness/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
